    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "'small joys' just feels like a distraction, like putting a band-aid on a gaping wound. it's just delaying the inevitable. if we're just accidental bits of matter that are eventually going to be crushed or burned out or forgotten, why does the struggle even matter? it feels like the only honest response to the void is to just stop fighting it. why should i keep pushing through all this pain if the end result is just zero?",
